# page word file line: the first occurrence of word on the page must be
# attributed by SyncTeX to that line of that file (see ../checksynctex.py).
# LuaTeX records font kerns, and the glyphs following them, with a stale
# position (that of the enclosing \input at shipout), in the main text as
# well; words right after a kerned word are therefore not checked here.
